   ]
  },
  {
   "statement": "No deployment records were found in the window, so there is no deploy lead. This rests on an empty query and is not proof that nothing changed.",
   "evidence_ids": [
    "src-deployments"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "unknowns": [
  "No metrics were collected for a checkout, payment or front-end service. The failing component may simply not be in the snapshot.",
  "The metrics only report the 5xx ratio. Checkout failures returned as 4xx, redirects, or 200s with error bodies would not show up here.",
  "The traces and logs queries returned nothing in the window even though services were serving traffic. This may mean instrumentation or the collection pipeline is broken, which hides any failure.",
  "Gateway traffic dipped near the end of the window (last 1.56 req/s against a 1.95 avg and 2.24 max), and orders and inventory also ended lower (1.10 against 1.33). This could mean customers are failing before they reach the gateway (DNS, CDN, load balancer, client), but the drop is modest and not conclusive.",
  "No deployment records were found. This rules out neither config or feature-flag changes nor deploys made outside the tracked pipeline."
 ],
 "recommended_actions": [
  {
   "action": "Collect HTTP metrics for any checkout, payment and front-end services, and break down gateway responses by route and status code, including 4xx.",
   "rationale": "The three measured services show no 5xx errors, so the failure is either in an unmeasured service or not visible as 5xx.",
   "evidence_ids": [
